{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "central_D1_nonuniform_zero_grad_bc_ast_fixture",
    "description": "AST-expansion conformance fixture for grids/cartesian_nonuniform_1d/rules/central_D1_nonuniform_zero_grad_bc: a minimal consuming model binding N=8 at the import edge. The plain match D(u,x) must fire through the section-9.6.3 fixpoint (default priority) and lower to the rule's makearray -- interior [2,7] holding the imported 3-point centered nonuniform first-derivative stencil aggregate, faces i=1 and i=8 holding the second-order one-sided nonuniform first derivatives -- with all metaparameters folded, all apply_expression_template nodes inlined (including the grid geometry template the observed xc applies to the node array xe), and the free-name geometry array xc surviving as index references. The model follows the grid's EDGE-ARRAY contract at N=8: it supplies the 9-node (x_nodes) quadratic-stretch array xe and derives xc = nonuniform_cell_center(xe), all spelled with the literal 8 because the edge binding closes N. A first derivative needs only the cell centers, so the control-width observed dxw is not materialized. The golden pins the byte-identical post-lowering AST across bindings.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "conformance",
      "ast",
      "grid:cartesian_nonuniform_1d",
      "rule:central_D1_nonuniform_zero_grad_bc"
    ]
  },
